Crashpad's ProcessID alias asserts it is exactly `int`, which fails to compile
on Haiku:

    static_assert(std::is_same<ProcessID, int>::value, "Port.");
    error: static assertion failed: Port.

Haiku's pid_t is `signed long int` (headers/config/types.h's __haiku_int32),
not `int`. The two are the same width on this 32-bit target -- so %d as
PRI_PROCESS_ID already prints it correctly, and nothing downstream that reads
ProcessID as a 32-bit value is wrong -- but they are distinct types to the
compiler, so std::is_same is false where it holds on every other POSIX target
this header supports.

The assert exists to catch a genuine width mismatch, so Haiku gets a width
check instead of a type-identity check, gated on OS_HAIKU (already defined by
build/build_config.h) rather than widening the general POSIX case.

This was unreached until 2026-08-30: nothing content_shell needs crashpad for
had been linked before, because is_linux is true for Haiku in this port
(build/config/BUILDCONFIG.gn) and crashpad's own BUILD.gn files gate most of
it on is_linux -- so this is the first Haiku build to compile crashpad's
process-identity code at all, not a regression.

--- a/chromium/third_party/crashpad/crashpad/util/process/process_id.h
+++ b/chromium/third_party/crashpad/crashpad/util/process/process_id.h
@@ -34,7 +34,18 @@
 //! \brief Alias for platform-specific type to represent a process.
 using ProcessID = pid_t;
 constexpr ProcessID kInvalidProcessID = -1;
+// Haiku's pid_t is "signed long int" (headers/config/types.h), not int -- the
+// two are the same width on this 32-bit target but are distinct types to the
+// compiler, so std::is_same<pid_t, int> is false here even though it holds on
+// every other POSIX platform this file supports. The assert exists to catch a
+// genuine width mismatch, which %d as PRI_PROCESS_ID would get wrong; long and
+// int being the same width on Haiku x86 means %d already prints it correctly,
+// so relaxing the assert for this one platform does not weaken what it checks.
+#if defined(OS_HAIKU)
+static_assert(sizeof(ProcessID) == sizeof(int), "Port.");
+#else
 static_assert(std::is_same<ProcessID, int>::value, "Port.");
+#endif
 #define PRI_PROCESS_ID "d"
 #elif defined(OS_WIN)
 using ProcessID = DWORD;
